    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0912" n="900" xml:id="pg900"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.96/7–2646: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Philippines</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McNutt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Manila</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-26T13:00:00+08:00">July 26, 1946—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 26—4:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. Following status treaties, conventions mentioned your telegram 79, July
                        22.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d687-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Military base agreement. President plans appoint Congress committee assist
                        negotiation. Studying provisions. Should move shortly.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Arbitration, conciliation, extradition and consular conventions under
                        study Foreign Office and informal discussion with Embassy. No
                        counter-proposals in prospect other than verbal changes. Expect agreement
                        shortly.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Income and inheritance tax conventions under study by Foreign Office which
                        has made no comment to date.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McNutt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
